  "source_id": "raw_html_a125d0ee1bd1013b",
  "source_identity": {
    "canonical_url": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/first-year/talcum-powder-for-babies",
    "source_record_id": "raw_html_a125d0ee1bd1013b",
    "udare_article_path": "C:\\Users\\HP\\Documents\\LinkCraftor\\backend\\server\\data\\udare_store\\ws_whattoexpect_com\\articles\\first-year-talcum-powder-for-babies_a125d0ee.html",
    "udare_article_sha256": "6d4395f29d6f511e66c9f36010e3e85ef33cb2f124ff732eae09f0e5abf24807"
  },
  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/first-year/talcum-powder-for-babies",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 27,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Is Baby Powder Safe to Use During Diaper Changes?",
        "text_sha256": "3a1e354bfc0c0b36fda7e27c1efe8bf90d74160304ed420ecde3742fc8e69413",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "mom diapering baby not using talcum powder",
        "text_sha256": "44ece681ac24da97142703bc1658a3f7801b7bb900ca08f7ae8912fd0277b501",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It has a scent that's become synonymous with babies . But are talc and other baby powders really necessary when you're changing diapers — and are they safe?",
        "text_sha256": "8cc7b53167a456261999ddd1ca186beea934a60a076b96ecc7ae2fe2e4d610d4",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "When many people picture babies, the first thing that comes to mind is their fresh baby scent — which might include a hint of baby powder. So what, exactly, is baby powder? And is it safe? Here’s what you need to know.",
        "text_sha256": "09bd022f6d473db19b034364b288af6edf8b26caca23369d292f4a0471ebe152",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "What is baby powder made of?",
        "text_sha256": "430d36f29aad585f4d31c92b701bd8f02d0e445635b5691043d517957db265e7",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Talcum-based baby powder is made from the mineral talc, which contains mostly the elements magnesium, silicon and oxygen. It absorbs moisture and reduces skin-on-skin friction, which may help prevent rashes, including diaper rash. That's why for many years, it was a staple on changing tables .",
        "text_sha256": "8d246f63b4d062dc445b4520b236b6ef0b8986c57d44937631cce6e150dec917",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But check the label, because many baby powders on the market today don't contain any talc at all. Numerous \"talc-free\" powders are made with cornstarch, another naturally absorbent ingredient, instead of talc. Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsHow to Choose Safer Personal Care Products: Tips for FamiliesSee All Sources [1]",
        "text_sha256": "6a692c618e6bf5b0a23c4fe7e7d249561edf03210b955b1da477956f6f7042f1",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsHow to Choose Safer Personal Care Products: Tips for FamiliesSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "38175281d9c79d9b7ff4592a7647c8a851d3fdf6de0bcd1658a5fbb0da255d18",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Types of baby powder: cornstarch baby powder vs. baby talcum powder",
        "text_sha256": "d784ec8b006d737eab7fbd309b5dbde5e1eff20d3f6e488f7ac0f886a6df299d",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The two main types of baby powder include cornstarch baby powder and baby talcum powder.",
        "text_sha256": "3e8c95e41817f9b274ab16dded5d8aed05cdbc8e3049510ac7323168ee429a39",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Baby talcum powder always contains two ingredients: talc (which absorbs moisture) and fragrance (which is what gives it that well-known baby scent). Cornstarch baby powder is made with cornstarch (another moisture-wicking ingredient) and the same baby-powder fragrance.",
        "text_sha256": "c3f0d628db551fc110688f3103cd5bca64fdc09d3f1f500f9182b0736c318f20",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Is baby powder safe?",
        "text_sha256": "1e00fe2100e38e83f2d143f9a003caf4e9dcbf69d0f7b4cc6a53d5157d14b16c",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP) recommends against using baby powder since babies don’t really need it (or most other lotions and oils, for that matter) and it can sometimes irritate their already-sensitive, delicate skin. Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsMake Baby's Room Safe: Parent ChecklistSee All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "cae0b3ef543a64487483dd678af5cde4bdbf71f5bfa1952603a969a733a0f017",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Academy of PediatricsMake Baby's Room Safe: Parent ChecklistSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "70ef07864908a6dc3709f84c6d6ed050e9eadace2762ba634929c06dbb61e93a",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The AAP also says that baby powder can be harmful to little ones if a lot is inhaled. What’s more, there has been concern over whether long-term use of talcum powder near the bikini line or genital area may put women at higher risk of ovarian cancer, as numerous lawsuits against powder manufacturers allege, and if regular exposure to talc increases the risk of ovarian cancer later.",
        "text_sha256": "6e5f562b73fdc539dab6c694e8cef197e4e266ec82b3f863734084ddfb04d2c7",
        "word_count": 67
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Although talcum products have been asbestos-free since the 1970s (in its natural form, talc contains some asbestos, which, when inhaled, is known to cause cancer), the link between asbestos-free talc and cancer, if any, remains unclear and studies have yielded mixed findings. Trusted SourceAmerican Cancer SocietyTalcum Powder and CancerSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "7a56179eb9e0fb812ba75d0d18c53a1592f1757ed63e54003950d52b8a6393b4",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican Cancer SocietyTalcum Powder and CancerSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "dac92af490d0f04608613c8467c88848572fac6a74348ddb93ded2e6fa03e664",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Cornstarch-based baby powders may be problematic too because their main ingredient may make a candida-caused diaper rash worse. Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, National Library of Medicine, Medline PlusCandida infection of the skinSee All Sources [4]",
        "text_sha256": "684854903ff4757d163ba3254dbca98eebf00a7beac3039a820dc5ccf027c4dd",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, National Library of Medicine, Medline PlusCandida infection of the skinSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "2e4beafeaf300c4a40e1084134f6b9071c1c9391b932ddd9803e8f900f94d250",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "For these reasons, it’s probably best to skip the baby powder — especially since there are other safer, effective ways to prevent diaper rash.",
        "text_sha256": "b375542544d184a091de389d55f7c28e7107acfd1081fcc57ac21a86235668f6",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "So how can I prevent diaper rash without baby powder?",
        "text_sha256": "15adff8c706d88b51de6c75a719f91e2f070f326a2f567610ad80adeac1e06ea",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Looking for alternatives to baby powder for protecting your little one’s sensitive diaper area?",
        "text_sha256": "15874dfeccb696b2551c32aed58f1c475d20ccdea6eefd439f86f0af972efb23",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here are a few tricks for preventing diaper rash :",
        "text_sha256": "61d7c9cd2373c598acd26bff35ed965f8b24bbc345e1f02b0c5641d606624f93",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Change her diaper frequently (and especially any time you suspect it’s dirty)",
        "text_sha256": "c90eeb188a4585b7bc48a398458e103e173df9a8af80f23a1e534b6198f9bcfb",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "If possible, give your baby’s bottom a minute to air out during diaper changes",
        "text_sha256": "16c6855bdbb3228ad62a961d0541fd8eb16a57d4af97038d1185bc36be69a915",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Once your child is totally dry, if she’s particularly prone to rashes, you may want to try using a petroleum- or zinc-oxide-based cream as a barrier for her sensitive skin",
        "text_sha256": "0f204d19f11dd9253b8b15b5e56577bbd041988379173974aff2e552fea28e1d",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you've already used baby powder of any kind on your little one, don't worry, since most baby powder on the market today is talc-free and talcum baby powder no longer contain asbestos (and hasn't for decades). Your best bet is just to steer clear of using a lot of baby powder on your child in the future.",
        "text_sha256": "10a47c546aeea558c3005c893db941c291b14a2450907721bdf79cbd13e27164",
        "word_count": 58
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 683,
    "heading_count": 5
  },
  "title": "Is Baby Powder Safe? What to Know About Talcum Powder & Babies",
